1
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:23,500
The fairytale is over

2
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Snow White and the Huntsman is a adventure, fantasy,
drama film directed by Rupert Sanders.

3
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:58,500
After the Evil Queen marries the King, she performs a violent coup in which the
King is murdered and his daughter, Snow White, is taken captive.

4
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Almost a decade later, a grown Snow White is still in the clutches of the Queen.

5
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:33,500
In order to obtain immortality, The Evil Queen needs the heart of Snow White.

6
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:51,000
After Snow escapes the castle, the Queen sends the
Huntsman to find her in the Dark Forest.

7
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:08,500
Snow White, played by Kristen Stewart.

8
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:26,000
The Huntsman, played by Chris Hemsworth.

9
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:43,500
Queen Ravenna, played by Charlize Theron.

10
00:52:55,000 --> 00:53:01,000
William, played by Sam Claflin.

11
00:58:12,500 --> 00:58:18,500
Beith, played by Ian McShane.

12
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Gort, played by Ray Winstone.

13
01:08:47,500 --> 01:08:53,500
Snow White & the Huntsman is a 2012 American dark fantasy action-adventure film directed by
Rupert Sanders and written by Evan Daugherty, John Lee Hancock, and Hossein Amini.

14
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:11,000
Produced by Roth Films and distributed by Universal Pictures, the film is based on the Brothers Grimm's 1812 fairy
tale "Snow White," and stars Kristen Stewart, Charlize Theron, Chris Hemsworth, and Sam Claflin.

15
01:19:22,500 --> 01:19:28,500
The plot follows princess Snow White, who grows up imprisoned by
her evil stepmother, the powerful sorceress Ravenna.

16
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
After Snow White escapes into the forest, Ravenna enlists a huntsman named Eric to capture her, but he
eventually becomes Snow White's companion in a quest to overthrow Ravenna and end her dark reign.

17
01:29:57,500 --> 01:30:03,500
Snow White & the Huntsman was theatrically released in the United Kingdom on May 30,
2012, and in the United States on June 1, 2012, by Universal Pictures.

18
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:21,000
The film was a box office success, having grossed $396.6
million worldwide against a $170 million budget.

19
01:40:32,500 --> 01:40:38,500
Critics praised the production design and visual effects, and Theron's and Hemsworth's performances, as well as James Newton
Howard's score, while the action sequences and Stewart's and Claflin's performances received mixed reviews.

20
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:56,000
The film received two Oscar nominations for Best Visual Effects and Best Costume Design at the
85th Academy Awards; Stewart won Worst Actress at the 33rd Golden Raspberry Awards.

21
01:51:07,500 --> 01:51:13,500
A sequel, titled The Huntsman: Winter's War, directed by the first film's visual effects supervisor Cedric
Nicolas-Troyan, was released on April 22, 2016, with Hemsworth, Theron, Claflin, and Nick Frost reprising their roles.

22
01:56:25,000 --> 01:56:31,000
The film explores themes of magic, immortality, fairy tale, queen, imprisonment.

23
02:01:42,500 --> 02:01:48,500
The tone is dark and emotional.
